From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 01:22:44 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] UefiPayloadPkg/CfrSetupMenuDxe: Link the setup password from
 a category

[ouroBIOS: patches/edk2/0003, without the files that TianoCore's tree
does not have (tools/edk2-import.py): 4 in edk2/OuroBiosPkg]

The password asked for before the setup menu opens is set in its own
formset, which UserAuthenticationDxe installs under System
Configuration, away from the security settings of the setup menu.

Add PcdCfrSetupMenuPasswordCategory: the title of the category of the
setup menu that ends with a card linking to that formset, "Security" by
default (an empty string leaves the link out). The link names the
formset by GUID. When UserAuthenticationDxe is not in the build, the
browser reports nothing: after the usual prompt about unsaved changes,
if any, selecting the link silently leaves the setup menu for the
previous formset, as for any goto to a missing formset.

TEST=QEMU q35: from the Security category the link opens the password
formset of UserAuthenticationDxe, and a 64-character password set there
opens the setup after a reboot; the setup of the W541 in the releases.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv

---
diff --git a/UefiPayloadPkg/UefiPayloadPkg.dec b/UefiPayloadPkg/UefiPayloadPkg.dec
index cf0b3269b..08119dc78 100644
--- a/UefiPayloadPkg/UefiPayloadPkg.dec
+++ b/UefiPayloadPkg/UefiPayloadPkg.dec
@@ -164,3 +164,8 @@ gUefiPayloadPkgTokenSpaceGuid.PcdPciAllocateMemoryAbove4GB|FALSE|BOOLEAN|0x00000
 #  default PK/KEK/db/dbx. If FALSE (legacy MrChromebox behavior), keys are
 #  enrolled but SecureBootEnable/SecureBoot remain disabled until toggled in setup.
 gUefiPayloadPkgTokenSpaceGuid.PcdSecureBootDefaultEnable|FALSE|BOOLEAN|0x0000002F
+
+## Title of the category of the CFR setup menu that ends with a link to the
+#  password asked for before the setup menu opens (UserAuthenticationDxe).
+#  An empty string leaves the link out.
+gUefiPayloadPkgTokenSpaceGuid.PcdCfrSetupMenuPasswordCategory|L"Security"|VOID*|0x00000030
-- 
2.43.0

